---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/legal.css';
---

<SiteLayout title="Coven Remote Support — OpenCoven" description="Set up macOS Screen Sharing, connect from iPhone or iPad, and get help with Coven Remote." canonicalPath="/remote/support">
  <section class="site-shell legal-page">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coven Remote</p>
      <h1>Your Mac, within reach.</h1>
      <p class="legal-lead">Control macOS Screen Sharing from iPhone or iPad with an adaptive keyboard and touchpad. Try the built-in demo before connecting a Mac.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="legal-panels">
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Connect your Mac</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>On your Mac, open System Settings → General → Sharing, turn on Screen Sharing, and allow the Mac user you intend to sign in as.</li>
          <li>Connect both devices through Tailscale or another trusted network. Keep the Mac awake and reachable.</li>
          <li>In Coven Remote, add your Mac's address and use the permitted Mac account credentials when prompted. The app does not require an OpenCoven account.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The app targets macOS Screen Sharing with Apple Remote Desktop authentication. It is not a general compatibility promise for every VNC server. VNC screen and input traffic is not encrypted by VNC itself; use a trusted encrypted network.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Keyboard, touchpad and displays</h2>
        <p>Use the Touchpad/Keyboard switch at the bottom of the input panel. More contains text entry, clipboard actions, monitor selection, modifiers and session controls. The fn key reveals function keys. The globe key opens Apple's composing keyboard, where swipe typing depends on your keyboard language and system settings.</p>
        <p>If macOS exposes one combined desktop, use Monitor to focus a region of that desktop. Fit keeps the whole desktop proportional, Fill crops to the available area, and Stretch fills the screen. Key sounds and subtle haptics are independently optional in Settings.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>If a connection fails</h2>
        <p>Check that Screen Sharing is enabled, the Mac is awake, the account is permitted and the address is reachable from your device. Check Tailscale on both devices when using it. Reconnect after changes. A non-Tailscale connection requires explicit approval; a saved password is not sent automatically on that route.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="legal-panel">
        <h2>Get help</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@opencoven.ai">hello@opencoven.ai</a> with Coven Remote in the subject, or use the <a href="https://feedback.opencoven.ai/hc">OpenCoven help center</a>. Include the app version, device and iOS version, macOS version, what you expected and steps to reproduce.</p>
        <p>Keep passwords, private Mac addresses, clipboard text and remote screen contents out of support messages and screenshots.</p>
        <p><a href="/remote/privacy">Coven Remote privacy policy</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
